{"schema":"SDW_SCRIPTURE_CHAPTER_V1","revision":"52add6f41edc5dd9c21f65f02f933fbd1cec266285bee8bce249607475050398","canonicalSourceHash":"f9dfbce6dd2edfe4bb3b4690acd6622f392035be2b0349df98f3607f0a05f6c2","bookId":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verses":[{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":925,"verse_start":1,"verse_end":1,"verse_label":"1","text":"Then the LORD answered Job out of the whirlwind,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2956},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":926,"verse_start":2,"verse_end":2,"verse_label":"2","text":"“Who is this who darkens counsel by words without knowledge?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2958},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":927,"verse_start":3,"verse_end":3,"verse_label":"3","text":"Brace yourself like a man, for I will question you, then you answer me!","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2961},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":928,"verse_start":4,"verse_end":4,"verse_label":"4","text":"“Where were you when I laid the foundations of the earth? Declare, if you have understanding.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2965},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":929,"verse_start":5,"verse_end":5,"verse_label":"5","text":"Who determined its measures, if you know? Or who stretched the line on it?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2968},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":930,"verse_start":6,"verse_end":6,"verse_label":"6","text":"What were its foundations fastened on? Or who laid its cornerstone,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2971},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":931,"verse_start":7,"verse_end":7,"verse_label":"7","text":"when the morning stars sang together, and all the sons of God shouted for joy?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2974},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":932,"verse_start":8,"verse_end":8,"verse_label":"8","text":"“Or who shut up the sea with doors, when it broke out of the womb,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2978},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":933,"verse_start":9,"verse_end":9,"verse_label":"9","text":"when I made clouds its garment, and wrapped it in thick darkness,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2981},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":934,"verse_start":10,"verse_end":10,"verse_label":"10","text":"marked out for it my bound, set bars and doors,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2984},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":935,"verse_start":11,"verse_end":11,"verse_label":"11","text":"and said, ‘You may come here, but no further. Your proud waves shall be stopped here’?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2987},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":936,"verse_start":12,"verse_end":12,"verse_label":"12","text":"“Have you commanded the morning in your days, and caused the dawn to know its place,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2991},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":937,"verse_start":13,"verse_end":13,"verse_label":"13","text":"that it might take hold of the ends of the earth, and shake the wicked out of it?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2994},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":938,"verse_start":14,"verse_end":14,"verse_label":"14","text":"It is changed as clay under the seal, and presented as a garment.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":2997},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":939,"verse_start":15,"verse_end":15,"verse_label":"15","text":"From the wicked, their light is withheld. The high arm is broken.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3000},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":940,"verse_start":16,"verse_end":16,"verse_label":"16","text":"“Have you entered into the springs of the sea? Or have you walked in the recesses of the deep?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3004},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":941,"verse_start":17,"verse_end":17,"verse_label":"17","text":"Have the gates of death been revealed to you? Or have you seen the gates of the shadow of death?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3007},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":942,"verse_start":18,"verse_end":18,"verse_label":"18","text":"Have you comprehended the earth in its width? Declare, if you know it all.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3010},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":943,"verse_start":19,"verse_end":19,"verse_label":"19","text":"“What is the way to the dwelling of light? As for darkness, where is its place,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3014},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":944,"verse_start":20,"verse_end":20,"verse_label":"20","text":"that you should take it to its bound, that you should discern the paths to its house?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3017},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":945,"verse_start":21,"verse_end":21,"verse_label":"21","text":"Surely you know, for you were born then, and the number of your days is great!","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3020},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":946,"verse_start":22,"verse_end":22,"verse_label":"22","text":"Have you entered the storehouses of the snow, or have you seen the storehouses of the hail,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3023},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":947,"verse_start":23,"verse_end":23,"verse_label":"23","text":"which I have reserved against the time of trouble, against the day of battle and war?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3026},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":948,"verse_start":24,"verse_end":24,"verse_label":"24","text":"By what way is the lightning distributed, or the east wind scattered on the earth?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3029},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":949,"verse_start":25,"verse_end":25,"verse_label":"25","text":"Who has cut a channel for the flood water, or the path for the thunderstorm,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3033},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":950,"verse_start":26,"verse_end":26,"verse_label":"26","text":"to cause it to rain on a land where there is no man, on the wilderness, in which there is no man,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3036},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":951,"verse_start":27,"verse_end":27,"verse_label":"27","text":"to satisfy the waste and desolate ground, to cause the tender grass to grow?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3039},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":952,"verse_start":28,"verse_end":28,"verse_label":"28","text":"Does the rain have a father? Or who fathers the drops of dew?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3042},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":953,"verse_start":29,"verse_end":29,"verse_label":"29","text":"Whose womb did the ice come out of? Who has given birth to the gray frost of the sky?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3045},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":954,"verse_start":30,"verse_end":30,"verse_label":"30","text":"The waters become hard like stone, when the surface of the deep is frozen.","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3048},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":955,"verse_start":31,"verse_end":31,"verse_label":"31","text":"“Can you bind the cluster of the Pleiades, or loosen the cords of Orion?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3052},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":956,"verse_start":32,"verse_end":32,"verse_label":"32","text":"Can you lead the constellations out in their season? Or can you guide the Bear with her cubs?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3055},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":957,"verse_start":33,"verse_end":33,"verse_label":"33","text":"Do you know the laws of the heavens? Can you establish its dominion over the earth?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3058},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":958,"verse_start":34,"verse_end":34,"verse_label":"34","text":"“Can you lift up your voice to the clouds, that abundance of waters may cover you?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3062},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":959,"verse_start":35,"verse_end":35,"verse_label":"35","text":"Can you send out lightnings, that they may go? Do they report to you, ‘Here we are’?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3065},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":960,"verse_start":36,"verse_end":36,"verse_label":"36","text":"Who has put wisdom in the inward parts? Or who has given understanding to the mind?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3068},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":961,"verse_start":37,"verse_end":37,"verse_label":"37","text":"Who can count the clouds by wisdom? Or who can pour out the containers of the sky,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3071},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":962,"verse_start":38,"verse_end":38,"verse_label":"38","text":"when the dust runs into a mass, and the clods of earth stick together?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3074},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":963,"verse_start":39,"verse_end":39,"verse_label":"39","text":"“Can you hunt the prey for the lioness, or satisfy the appetite of the young lions,","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3078},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":964,"verse_start":40,"verse_end":40,"verse_label":"40","text":"when they crouch in their dens, and lie in wait in the thicket?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3081},{"translation_id":"engwebu","book_id":"engwebu:job","chapter":38,"verse_ordinal":965,"verse_start":41,"verse_end":41,"verse_label":"41","text":"Who provides for the raven his prey, when his young ones cry to God, and wander for lack of food?","is_omitted":0,"source_line":3084}]}